      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e On Eve this issue is preventing cr50 from reentering deep sleep. \n\u003e This means in G3 cr50 will go into deep sleep for about an hour.\n\u003e It will wake up after an hour to reset TIMERLS0 and\n\u003e then it will never reenter deep sleep\n\nthis might just be the existing race condition in the __idle() inner while loop, e.g. :\nyou might check the sleep_ok condition (or the other conditions there before the prepare_to_sleep, find a negative result\nthen be de-scheduled by the real work,\ncome back to idle when all the work is done,\nas the condition is negative,do a simple wfi without sleep/deep-sleep\nand stay there since there is no longer any wake-up to do.\n\nThe usleep() would solve this by doing one more iteration of the iteration while loop and re-evaluate properly the sleep conditions.\n\nif you look at other low-power sleep modes implementation we did, all the sleep conditions evaluation is done interrupts disabled to avoid this race condition, e.g. :\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/chip/stm32/clock-stm32f0.c#310\n\nThis is just a random idea about this issue, but the __idle() code is definitely wrong in some corner cases.",
      "parentUuid": "46cd54ea_5372e2a0",
      "range": {
